{"title":"Tuesday assorted links","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/912759722/0/marginalrevolution~Tuesday-assorted-links.html","date":1739293348000,"content":"<p>1. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/papers/w33446#fromrss\" target=\"_blank\">How much did the modern mortgage support the baby boom?</a></p>\r\n<p>2. “<a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/papers/w33441#fromrss\" target=\"_blank\">Over the 2008-2016 period, the global cycle phase, the North accounts for 68% of Southern [bond] spreads’ fluctuations. Over the whole 1994-2024 period, however, Northern shocks account for less than 20% of these fluctuations.</a>”</p>\r\n<p>3. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/bevansadvocate/status/1888694222565556471?s=48\" target=\"_blank\">Adam Smith cartoon</a>.</p>\r\n<p>4. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.betonit.ai/p/tell-us-a-childhood-story-part-1\" target=\"_blank\">Bryan Caplan is telling childhood stories, and thus making it possible for the AIs to write his biography</a>.  I plan to do a bit of the same.</p>\r\n<p>5. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://goodscience.substack.com/p/indirect-costs-at-nih?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=1010915&amp;post_id=156756159&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=3o9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\">Stuart Buck argues the indirect cost rates at the NIH are protected by current law</a>.</p>\r\n<p>6. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://economistwritingeveryday.com/2025/02/10/is-there-a-competitive-threat-to-the-nba/\" target=\"_blank\">Did the Saudis raise the return to trading Luka?</a></p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolutio